WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.690
Narrator: The new trailer
for "Detective Pikachu"

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.740
is full of recognizable Pokémon
from the classic series,

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:12.290
and you have to look carefully
if you wanna catch them all.

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.010
Here's a look at everything
you might have missed.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.140
The film stars Ryan Reynolds as Pikachu,

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:19.440
And is this a subtle reference

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.720
to another Ryan Reynolds
character, Green Lantern?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.460
Pikachu: Another round, extra shot,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.810
blackest night, thank you sweetie.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.220
Narrator: "Blackest Night" is the name

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.510
of a "Green Lantern" comic series.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.380
The movie takes place in
the fictional Ryme City,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.940
the same city in the Nintendo 3DS game,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.390
and the plot revolves around Pikachu

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.680
and a boy named Tim Goodman

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.840
searching for his father Harry Goodman,

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.970
who disappeared after
a mysterious car crash.

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.220
Kathryn Newton from "Big Little Lies"

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:51.720
plays a character named Lucy,
seen here with her Psyduck.

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.820
The shots of Ryme City
are full of references

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:56.870
to various Pokémon from
different generations.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:01:00.070
Here's a Snorlax sleeping
at an intersection,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.330
a shout-out to the games
in which the Snorlax

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.850
usually blocks the player's path.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:07.400
Machamp seems to be directing traffic

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.240
with his multiple arms.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.640
Outside the RCPD building,
we see multiple police dogs,

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.810
Growlithe and the evolved form Arcanine.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.060
There's also what appears to be a Slaking

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:21.060
lying in the background,

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.403
and Gen V's Golurk working
as security guards.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.540
Climbing on the power lines
outside of this building

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:32.683
are some Joltik, bug-electric-type
Pokémon from Gen V.

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.240
In the game, the Hi-Hat Café

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.110
is owned by a character
named Pablo Millan,

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:41.410
and his Pokémon Ludicolo seen here.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.580
Ludicolo: Ludicolo!

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.420
Narrator: The sign outside
the café shows the owl Pokémon

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:50.170
Noctowl, which makes sense
since it's a nocturnal creature.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:54.100
We see a very furry Jigglypuff
on the table in the café,

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:56.173
which also appeared in the first trailer.

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:00.150
And behind it is a poster
for an upcoming battle

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:02.720
between two fighting-type Pokémon.

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.363
Machamp and Primeape.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:08.680
Mr. Mime was also featured
in the first trailer

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.010
with his disturbing new look,

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:14.090
and he's still being
interrogated by Tim and Pikachu.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.147
We also see some quick shots
of a slobbery Lickitung

00:02:17.147 --> 00:02:19.170
and a grumpy looking Snubull.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:21.080
The trailer give us our first glimpse

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:23.283
of a Pokémon battle arena as well.

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:26.904
Flanking the DJs are two Loudred Pokémon,

00:02:26.904 --> 00:02:30.730
which have ears that
work like loudspeakers.

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.920
The two Pokémon fighting
appear to be Blastoise

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.723
and the ghost-type Pokémon Gengar.

00:02:37.350 --> 00:02:40.330
And if you look closely,
there's even a Magikarp

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:42.340
in the fish tank in the background.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.098
We get a quick shot of many other Pokémon,

00:02:44.106 --> 00:02:46.581
watching from the sidelines.

00:02:46.581 --> 00:02:50.580
Behind Pikachu is Pancham,
a panda-like Pokémon

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.060
we also saw on a missing persons poster

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:55.120
next to a missing Squirtle.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:58.270
There's also a Charmander and a Treecko.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.600
And in the wide shot, we
see what appears to be

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.750
Audino and Octillery.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.032
Pikachu gets paired up against Charizard,

00:03:05.032 --> 00:03:08.130
whose trainer also has a
Charizard tattoo on his chest.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:12.005
There's a brief shot of a
large building in a valley,

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:15.045
this is likely the Pokémon
Comprehensive Laboratory

00:03:15.045 --> 00:03:16.236
from the video game,

00:03:16.236 --> 00:03:19.062
a key location in the plot of the story,

00:03:19.062 --> 00:03:20.187
which we won't spoil here.

00:03:22.103 --> 00:03:25.015
Here we see Tim and Pikachu
being led through a stream

00:03:25.015 --> 00:03:28.005
by a bunch of Bulbasaur and Morelull.

00:03:28.005 --> 00:03:31.133
And a Cubone, which wears
the skull of its dead mother,

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.108
pops out of a Pokéball.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.146
There are a few different shots

00:03:35.146 --> 00:03:38.183
of a monkey fighting-type
Pokémon called Aipom,

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:40.045
which look a lot more vicious

00:03:40.045 --> 00:03:42.580
than they do in the games or cartoon.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:45.950
On the desk next to Pikachu,
we see three stones.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.970
These are likely evolution stones,

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.410
which are used to evolve certain Pokémon.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:53.470
The one in the middle
resembles the Sinnoh Stone,

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.960
a Gen IV stone exclusive to Pokémon Go.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.310
Speaking of evolutions,

00:03:58.310 --> 00:04:00.360
the trailer also shows us an Eevee

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:04.080
evolving into a fire-type
Pokémon, Flareon.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.078
And behind this Flareon are statues

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:08.141
of Dialga, Arceus, and Palkia

00:04:08.144 --> 00:04:09.160
from left to right.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:14.013
Ryme City is famous for
hosting a Pokémon carnival,

00:04:14.013 --> 00:04:17.083
and these parade balloons
likely appear during this event.

00:04:17.092 --> 00:04:20.075
We get our first look at
the legendary Gen I Pokémon

00:04:20.083 --> 00:04:24.091
Mewtwo emerging from
one of these balloons.

00:04:24.091 --> 00:04:26.065
Mewtwo also plays a very important role

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:27.201
in the story, but you'll have to wait

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:30.707
until the film comes out in
May to solve the mystery.

00:04:30.707 --> 00:04:32.015
Tim: He's barely moving.

00:04:32.015 --> 00:04:33.148
Pikachu: Don't tell him that.

00:04:33.148 --> 00:04:35.107
Oh, he's on a bike, quick,
get in front of him.

00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:36.981
Tim: Stop.

00:04:36.989 --> 00:04:39.073
Pikachu: Oh no, he's going down hard, Tim.

00:04:39.082 --> 00:04:40.192
Shoulda worn a helmet.

